It is noon and I am hungry.
I walk to the bakery on the corner.
The bakery is very busy.
Many people are buying their lunch here.
I wait a few minutes.
Then it is my turn.
"Good afternoon, what would you like?" asks the baker.
"Good afternoon, I would like a cheese bread roll and a black tea, please," I answer.
"Gladly."
"Are you eating here?" he asks.
"No, to take away," I say.
"That makes four Euro fifty, then," says the baker.
I pay with a ten Euro note.
The baker gives me my change.
He also gives me the receipt.
"Thank you very much and goodbye," I say.
"Goodbye and have a nice day," he answers.
I go back outside.
The sun is shining so beautifully today.
I sit down on a bench.
I drink my tea and eat the bread roll in the sun.
